---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import ToolEmbed from '../components/ToolEmbed.astro';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="AI Sovereignties"
  description="A live map of the infrastructure behind AI in Australia, and the public debate forming around it. Data centres, mines, refineries, energy and water, and the lines of ownership running through them."
  ogImage="/images/og-sovereignties.png"
  dataset={{
    name: "Australia's Critical AI Infrastructure Tracker",
    description: "A live, openly maintained map of the infrastructure behind AI in Australia: data centres, rare-earth mines, refineries, and the energy and water they draw, with ownership, approval pathways, and the public contestation forming around each site.",
    keywords: ["AI sovereignty", "data centres", "critical minerals", "AI infrastructure", "Australia", "compute", "rare earths"],
    spatialCoverage: "Australia",
  }}
>
  <main class="container sov">

    <header class="sov-header">
      <p class="sov-eyebrow">Civic Interplay / Sovereignties</p>
      <h1>AI Sovereignties</h1>
      <p class="sov-intro">
        A live map of the infrastructure behind AI in Australia, and the public
        debate forming around it. Data centres, mines, refineries, the energy
        and water they draw, and the lines of ownership running through them.
        Each point is a real site on the ground.
      </p>
    </header>

    <ToolEmbed
      title="Mapping AI Sovereignties"
      src="https://sovereignties.civicinterplay.io/"
      openLabel="Open the map in a new tab"
      height="820px"
    />
    <p class="sov-note">
      Not loading? Your browser may be blocking the embedded site. Use the <a href="https://sovereignties.civicinterplay.io/" target="_blank" rel="noopener external">open in a new tab</a> link to launch it directly.
    </p>

    <section class="sov-section">
      <h2>What you're looking at</h2>
      <p>
        Every point is a site: a data centre, a mine, a refinery, or a piece of
        energy or water infrastructure. The colours trace ownership and
        governance, who owns it, who approved it, and what it draws to keep
        running. The map reads from an open tracker, so it shifts as the tracker
        does.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="sov-section">
      <h2>The debate, not just the opposition</h2>
      <p>
        Alongside the map we track contestation: the public record of who is
        arguing about these sites, on what grounds, and how intensely. It holds
        the case for as well as against. Jobs, investment and sovereign
        capability on one side; water, energy, consultation and amenity on the
        other.
      </p>
      <p>
        One pattern we watch is the lag, how long after a project is approved
        before any public contestation appears. Where a foreign-owned site
        carrying a sovereignty claim draws none at all, the silence is itself the
        finding.
      </p>
      <p>
        <a href="https://studio-esem.notion.site/Contestation-sovereignty-trackers-full-session-38d18df0b77581f697dfe059a69b454d" target="_blank" rel="noopener external">See the contestation record</a>, the trackers behind the map, in Notion.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="sov-section">
      <h2>The rise of a term</h2>
      <p>
        "AI sovereignty" went from near-absent to everywhere in three years. The chart below captures
        how often it appears in global news coverage. Close to zero in 2022, a spike
        around Davos in early 2025, and a peak through 2026.
      </p>
      <img
        class="sov-chart"
        src="/images/ai-sovereignty-timeline.svg"
        alt="Line chart of global news coverage mentioning 'sovereign AI' or 'AI sovereignty', rising from near-zero in 2022 to a peak in 2026."
        loading="lazy"
      />
      <p class="sov-chart-credit">
        Source: GDELT news-coverage volume (relative),
        <a href="https://app.notion.com/p/38e18df0b77581f5a06cd1b03bfd4707" target="_blank" rel="noopener external">data and method</a>.
        More in the
        <a href="https://studio-esem.notion.site/AI-Sovereignties-project-explainer-38d18df0b77581ab8465dcb65a6628ad" target="_blank" rel="noopener external">project explainer</a>.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="sov-section">
      <h2>Where the data comes from</h2>
      <p>
        The map sources data from a Critical Infrastructure Tracker, a
        database built in Notion. The data is sourced agentically, supported through Claude Code, with compute costs also tracked recursively. The contestation record is built from
        planning submissions, local and national press, local governments and other inquiry
        material. Corrections are welcome; the effort feels gestural rather than comprehensive, for now.
      </p>
      <p>
        Spot a missing site, an error, or contestation we have not captured? <a href="https://studio-esem.notion.site/a504252cf109454598a7b02e5024b10d" target="_blank" rel="noopener external">Submit it here</a>.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="sov-section">
      <h2>Methods, citation and licence</h2>
      <p>
        Formally, this is <em>a living atlas of contested AI sovereignties (Australian version)</em>. How each entry is sourced and classified is set out in the <a href="https://studio-esem.notion.site/AI-Sovereignties-project-explainer-38d18df0b77581ab8465dcb65a6628ad" target="_blank" rel="noopener external">project explainer</a>. Entries are coded by agent and flagged for human review (agent, human, or human-verified), so the basis of each classification stays visible.
      </p>
      <p>
        The project's methodology, classification and written analysis are openly licensed under <a href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/" target="_blank" rel="noopener external">CC BY 4.0</a>. The underlying records are compiled from public sources, cited per entry; the facts themselves carry no such claim. Cite as: Sarah Barns, <em>A living atlas of contested AI sovereignties (Australian version)</em>, Civic Interplay, 2026. <a href="https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.21026430" target="_blank" rel="noopener external">doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.21026430</a>.
      </p>
    </section>

    <aside class="sov-cost">
      <p class="sov-cost-label">The cost of this research</p>
      <p>
        This project runs on AI too. Across five working sessions it has used <em>roughly</em> the
        energy of <strong>12 phone charges</strong>, <strong>one and a half glasses</strong>
        of water, and the carbon of a <strong>350 m car trip</strong> (about 156 Wh, 358 mL
        and 64 g CO₂). The compute costs are self-reported by Claude Code, and probably very unreliable? They are logged openly in the
        <a href="https://studio-esem.notion.site/10618c7776a749fb8051ee4e8d1df570?v=4b15487e90c245358d7cae4d7c85cd89" target="_blank" rel="noopener external">Cost of Compute tracker</a>.
        Rough estimates; snapshot 29 June 2026.
      </p>
    </aside>

    <footer class="sov-footer">
      <p>
        Find this map alongside the other tools on the <a href="/doing">Do page</a>.
        Questions or corrections? <a href="https://sarahbarns.com" rel="external">Reach out</a>.
      </p>
      <p>
        Presented at the American Association of Geographers Annual Conference, San Francisco, April 2026. <a href="/aag-barns-2026.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener">View the slides (PDF)</a>.
      </p>
    </footer>

  </main>

  <style>
    .sov {
      padding: 3rem 2rem 4rem;
      max-width: 880px;
    }

    .sov-header {
      margin-bottom: 2.5rem;
      padding-bottom: 2rem;
      border-bottom: 2px solid var(--border);
    }

    .sov-eyebrow {
      font-family: var(--heading);
      font-size: 0.7rem;
      font-weight: 500;
      letter-spacing: 0.12em;
      text-transform: uppercase;
      color: var(--text-faint);
      margin-bottom: 0.6rem;
    }

    .sov-header h1 {
      font-family: var(--heading);
      font-size: clamp(2rem, 5vw, 3rem);
      font-weight: 300;
      letter-spacing: 0.04em;
      text-transform: uppercase;
      margin-bottom: 0.6rem;
    }

    .sov-intro {
      font-family: var(--body);
      font-size: 0.95rem;
      font-style: italic;
      color: var(--text-dim);
      max-width: 62ch;
    }

    .sov-note {
      font-family: var(--heading);
      font-size: 0.78rem;
      color: var(--text-faint);
      margin-top: 1rem;
      max-width: 65ch;
    }

    .sov-note a {
      color: var(--text-dim);
      text-decoration: underline;
      text-underline-offset: 3px;
    }

    .sov-note a:hover {
      color: var(--purple);
    }

    .sov-section {
      margin-top: 3rem;
    }

    .sov-section h2 {
      font-family: var(--heading);
      font-size: clamp(1.4rem, 3vw, 2rem);
      font-weight: 400;
      letter-spacing: 0.04em;
      margin-bottom: 0.8rem;
    }

    .sov-section p {
      font-family: var(--body);
      font-size: 1rem;
      line-height: 1.7;
      color: var(--text);
      max-width: 65ch;
      margin-bottom: 1rem;
    }

    .sov-section p a {
      color: var(--purple);
      text-decoration: underline;
      text-underline-offset: 3px;
    }

    .sov-footer {
      margin-top: 3.5rem;
      padding-top: 2rem;
      border-top: 2px solid var(--border);
    }

    .sov-footer p {
      font-family: var(--body);
      font-size: 0.95rem;
      color: var(--text-dim);
      max-width: 60ch;
    }

    .sov-footer a {
      color: var(--purple);
      text-decoration: underline;
      text-underline-offset: 3px;
    }

    .sov-chart {
      display: block;
      width: 100%;
      height: auto;
      margin-top: 1.25rem;
      border: 2px solid var(--border);
      border-radius: var(--radius);
      box-shadow: 4px 4px 0 var(--border);
      background: #fafafa;
    }

    .sov-section p.sov-chart-credit {
      font-family: var(--heading);
      font-size: 0.78rem;
      color: var(--text-faint);
      margin-top: 0.8rem;
    }

    .sov-section p.sov-chart-credit a {
      color: var(--purple);
      text-decoration: underline;
      text-underline-offset: 3px;
    }

    .sov-cost {
      margin-top: 3rem;
      border: 2px solid var(--border);
      border-left: 4px solid #D16D54;
      background: #faf6f0;
      border-radius: var(--radius);
      box-shadow: 4px 4px 0 var(--border);
      padding: 1.25rem 1.5rem;
    }

    .sov-cost-label {
      font-family: var(--heading);
      font-size: 0.7rem;
      font-weight: 500;
      letter-spacing: 0.12em;
      text-transform: uppercase;
      color: var(--text-faint);
      margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
    }

    .sov-cost p:last-child {
      font-family: var(--body);
      font-size: 0.95rem;
      line-height: 1.7;
      color: var(--text);
      max-width: 65ch;
      margin: 0;
    }

    .sov-cost a {
      color: var(--purple);
      text-decoration: underline;
      text-underline-offset: 3px;
    }

    @media (max-width: 640px) {
      .sov {
        padding: 2rem 1rem 3rem;
      }
    }
  </style>
</BaseLayout>
